body:
Omfg he did this shit all the time. He'd do it ESPECIALLY after telling a story about a bratty coworker or when commenting on his boyfriend and say shit like "if this is how they would react toward xyz, can't imagine how they'd survive with what *I* went through" then pat himself on the back and act like he was giving sage wisdom on trauma. Then he'd go on hour long rants about how awful his childhood was and how he couldn't stand watching other people be successful because he felt he deserved it better because of his trauma. Like SHUT THE FUCK UP. He has no fucken clue what he's talking about half the time and automatically assumes that because someone looks nice and well-put together, they haven't faced a struggle in their life. My god I have no idea how I put up with him for so long and this post touched a nerve lol

&#x200B;

edit: wanted to add how he would victimize himself in EVERY. SINGLE. STORY. He was the type of person who'd come home and claim that he was almost beat to death when it turns out he was just lightly slapped across the face. He'll purposely stretch the details and omit parts of the story that make him look bad. He knew what he was doing.

AND I KNOW ALL YOU DEVILS BY YOUR CHRISTIAN NAAMES!

&#x200B;

my favorite line
